<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 up 3.05 pct, M2 down 1.45 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 up 3.05 pct, M2 down 1.45 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to 601.4 billion levs on April 18 from 583.6 billion levs a week earlier and M2 edged down to 3,045 billion levs from 3,089.8 billion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money fell 1.98 percent to 3,217.9 billion levs in the week to April 18.</p>
<p>Conversion of dollar-denominated deposits into levs was made at an exchange rate of 1,500.3 levs per dollar on April 18 against 1,560.9 on April 11.  </p>
